# Final Bell

- Product display name: Final Bell. New native module: FinalBell. Python prefix: final_bell.
- Read the relevant requirements in FinalBell_Cursor_Master_Prompt.md and docs/FinalBell_Design_Review_and_Decisions.md. The longer renamed reference preserves future scope; the review resolves conflicts. Latest user instructions take precedence.
- Keep gameplay first: training, AI sparring and 1v1 multiplayer; preserve stamina, swelling/cuts/blood, server-controlled flash KOs and readable boxing records.
- FB-ENH-01 through FB-ENH-06 are required phased features: signature defense, explanatory flash-KO replay, actionable training feedback, uncertain scouting cards, explorable records/rank-change explanations, and private rooms/one ranked pool/later fight nights and league tools. Track status and evidence in docs/FeatureStatus.md. Do not treat these six as optional or claim they are implemented from documentation alone.
- Plan for multiplayer from the start. P1 includes an authoritative two-client combat proof; public ranked services are a later gate.
- Native Unreal C++ owns frame-critical combat. Python world/reference/backend code must not run in the combat frame loop. Editor Python is not packaged gameplay.
- Server validates intents and owns hits, resources, referee state and result. Clients never supply authoritative damage or wins.
- Keep true ability, scouting, readiness, player MMR, fighter merit ranking and title eligibility distinct.
- Isolate offline/official and traditional/VR state by domain/universe. Do not import local stats into official competition.
- Exact seeded replay is for pinned headless models. Real-time replay uses authoritative events/snapshots and compatible UE recording; do not assume cross-build physics determinism.
- Two people: one owner and one reviewer per task; agree versioned contracts and avoid concurrent edits to shared binary assets. Preserve existing work.
- Implement the current milestone in small compilable increments. Update docs/Progress.md with real tests, blockers and next action.
- Inspect installed APIs/plugins and actual assets. Never invent .uasset files, source inspections, test results or completed editor operations.
- Treat referenced FightVantage reuse as unverified until the exact commit, permissions, dependencies and tests are inspected. Preserve that independent project's name.
- Existing module/class renames need asset/save compatibility and redirects. Change branding without breaking necessary legacy references.
- Other optional suggestions, promotion depth, extensive world scale, console and VR remain gated backlog items; this does not downgrade the six FB-ENH requirements.
